1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,132
The relieving watchstander needs to know what remains unresolved, and where the evidence is.

2
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:18,179
Eight Bells is a focused watch-turnover tool: it reads the log, flags what needs a second look, and drafts the turnover with a source line behind every point.

3
00:00:18,179 --> 00:00:19,927
Today's log is synthetic.

4
00:00:20,177 --> 00:00:21,912
Here is how it works.

5
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:31,242
Everything runs on this one computer: the page in your browser, a small PowerShell server on loopback, and a launcher you double-click.

6
00:00:31,242 --> 00:00:32,869
Closing the tab stops the server.

7
00:00:33,569 --> 00:00:40,426
Records live in an encrypted store for your Windows account, with a hash-chained audit trail.

8
00:00:41,213 --> 00:00:48,608
Watch logs go in: text, CSV, JSON, tables, XML, and the text layer of digital PDFs.

9
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:54,322
Out come findings and a turnover draft, built offline by rules, with no AI.

10
00:00:54,322 --> 00:00:57,358
Every point links to its line in the log.

11
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,259
An AI briefing is optional.

12
00:01:00,259 --> 00:01:03,551
The model key sits in Lazarette, shared to Fairlead.

13
00:01:03,551 --> 00:01:09,959
Eight Bells has its own Fairlead key, and requests stay local-only unless you say otherwise.

14
00:01:10,659 --> 00:01:17,584
Reviewed lessons can go to Halyard as a hand-off file, and counts go to Semaphore as a CSV.

15
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:21,971
Not built yet: OCR for scans, and vendor log formats.

16
00:01:22,671 --> 00:01:31,807
And the guardrails: loopback only, drafts tied to their source, AI only when you consent, and every finding needs a person.

17
00:01:32,198 --> 00:01:35,764
To use the AI briefing, give Eight Bells its own key.

18
00:01:35,764 --> 00:01:41,171
In Fairlead, open Clients, and choose Install for an app.

19
00:01:41,871 --> 00:01:43,643
Name it EightBells and install.

20
00:01:44,343 --> 00:01:48,217
Fairlead makes the key and saves it straight to Windows Credential Manager.

21
00:01:48,917 --> 00:01:50,005
It is never shown.

22
00:01:50,705 --> 00:01:56,661
Fairlead's OpenAI connection already takes its key from Lazarette, so the provider key never touches Eight Bells.

23
00:01:57,361 --> 00:02:02,592
Back in Eight Bells, the router card shows Fairlead answering, and its own key installed.

24
00:02:02,592 --> 00:02:06,059
Start with an empty store, and import a log.

25
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:11,007
This one is a simulated engineering watch, marked synthetic in its first line.

26
00:02:11,707 --> 00:02:17,729
The preview shows every entry with its time, its equipment and its source line number, before anything is saved.

27
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:19,968
Import, and it is stored encrypted.

28
00:02:19,968 --> 00:02:22,364
Quality review found three advisory findings.

29
00:02:22,364 --> 00:02:26,562
They are prompts to check the record, not conclusions.

30
00:02:27,262 --> 00:02:34,635
The first is an entry out of sequence: line eight is a late entry, logged after a later time.

31
00:02:34,635 --> 00:02:36,781
Each finding shows its source lines.

32
00:02:37,481 --> 00:02:43,759
The second is a possible unresolved condition: Pump B vibration stays open from the first line to the last.

33
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:46,856
A reviewer records a disposition and a reason.

34
00:02:47,556 --> 00:02:49,753
The review is recorded beside the finding.

35
00:02:50,466 --> 00:02:52,385
The source log is never changed.

36
00:02:52,385 --> 00:02:54,025
Now the turnover, offline.

37
00:02:54,025 --> 00:02:58,277
This browser can reach nothing but this computer, and AI is off.

38
00:02:58,977 --> 00:03:00,024
Generate the draft.

39
00:03:00,024 --> 00:03:07,355
The rules engine writes it in an instant: observations, open conditions, and quality findings.

40
00:03:08,055 --> 00:03:13,151
Select any line number and the source line opens below, in the log exactly as imported.

41
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:15,415
That is the evidence trail.

42
00:03:15,665 --> 00:03:17,197
Now the stale-draft guard.

43
00:03:17,705 --> 00:03:19,329
Generate a draft for this log.

44
00:03:19,946 --> 00:03:22,785
Then the log is corrected, and a new version is imported.

45
00:03:23,485 --> 00:03:26,449
Select the corrected log and the old draft is gone.

46
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:28,770
Copy and Save are disabled.

47
00:03:29,279 --> 00:03:32,188
A draft cannot be exported once its source has changed.

48
00:03:32,888 --> 00:03:36,147
Even going back to the original does not bring it back.

49
00:03:36,147 --> 00:03:40,261
Generate again, and the draft is rebuilt from the source as it is now.

50
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:44,082
Now the optional AI briefing, through Fairlead.

51
00:03:44,082 --> 00:03:47,885
The card shows Fairlead answering and the key installed.

52
00:03:47,885 --> 00:03:52,067
Keep requests on this PC is ticked, so only local models may answer.

53
00:03:52,767 --> 00:03:56,031
Ask for a draft with the consent box ticked.

54
00:03:56,031 --> 00:04:02,528
No local model is loaded on this PC, so Fairlead refuses, and nothing leaves the machine.

55
00:04:02,528 --> 00:04:03,878
Eight Bells says why.

56
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:08,528
For synthetic data only, untick it and name a model.

57
00:04:08,528 --> 00:04:11,954
Fairlead may now use a cloud model, under that provider's terms.

58
00:04:12,654 --> 00:04:14,865
Same request, now with cloud allowed.

59
00:04:15,565 --> 00:04:21,986
A real answer in about two seconds, marked unverified, citing line numbers to check against the log.

60
00:04:22,686 --> 00:04:31,304
Fairlead's Activity page shows both calls from the client EightBells: one refused as private, one served by OpenAI's gpt-4.

61
00:04:31,304 --> 00:04:31,718
1-mini.

62
00:04:31,718 --> 00:04:37,350
Across the two logs, Eight Bells notices that Pump B stays open, and suggests a lesson.

63
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:40,437
Save it as a draft, then mark it reviewed.

64
00:04:40,437 --> 00:04:43,543
That mark is local, not a signed approval.

65
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:45,089
Export it for Halyard.

66
00:04:45,789 --> 00:04:48,138
Halyard's Intake reads that file through its API.

67
00:04:48,138 --> 00:04:51,182
It returns a story draft linked back to the lesson.

68
00:04:51,182 --> 00:04:54,671
Preview only, nothing written to the backlog.

69
00:04:54,671 --> 00:04:57,673
There is no button for it in Halyard's page yet.

70
00:04:58,373 --> 00:05:05,890
Counts per watch go to Semaphore as a CSV: logs, open conditions, findings, lessons.

71
00:05:05,890 --> 00:05:06,517
No log text.

72
00:05:06,517 --> 00:05:11,288
That is Eight Bells: a focused watch-turnover capability.

73
00:05:11,288 --> 00:05:17,064
It tells the relieving watch what is open, and where the evidence is.

74
00:05:17,064 --> 00:05:24,012
The log was synthetic, the findings are advisory, and a person verifies everything.

75
00:05:24,012 --> 00:05:24,933
Fair winds.
